; Control bytes in a diagnostic message, and the three renderers that
; have to survive them.
;
; A macro rule's accepted SHAPE is the author's own pattern spelling,
; joined from the tokens the pattern consumed - so for a string
; literal it is a SOURCE SLICE, carrying whatever bytes the file
; holds. That is the route by which a control byte reaches a message
; from a program that is otherwise well-formed, and it is why this
; fixture is a macro rather than the one-line `data` declaration that
; first exposed it: the grammar has to accept every `.ax` file in the
; repository (scripts/check-tree-sitter.sh), so a fixture whose error
; is a PARSE error cannot live here.
;
; Three independent bugs, one byte. All found 2026-08-16.
;
;   AXDL (self_host/diag.ax, `quoteBody`) escaped newline, tab and
;   carriage return and passed every other control byte through RAW,
;   on the recorded ground that anything else "can only reach a
;   lexeme as an ESCAPE". A source slice falsifies that. AXDL's
;   contract is that it is colourless and greppable, and a raw byte
;   is neither - a raw ESC would let a lexeme write terminal escape
;   sequences into any consumer that prints the line.
;
;   JSON (self_host/render.ax, `jsonEsc`) escaped only the quote, the
;   backslash and newline. RFC 8259 forbids a raw byte below 0x20
;   inside a string, so this one byte was enough to emit JSON that no
;   parser accepts - and nothing noticed, because the golden held the
;   same bad bytes. `check-render-selfhost.sh` now PARSES the JSON
;   rather than only diffing it, which is the half a re-bless cannot
;   satisfy.
;
;   HUMAN (self_host/render.ax, `ctlEsc`) printed the message, label,
;   notes and helps verbatim. That surface goes to a TERMINAL, so it
;   is the one where a raw ESC matters most - the renderer's colours
;   are style.ax's to choose, not a lexeme's.
;
; The byte is 0x01, which has a two-character escape in none of the
; three formats and so takes the `\u{1}` form in AXDL and human and
; the four-hex-digit form in JSON. It is deliberately the ONLY
; control byte here, because each of the three AXDL spells in two
; characters is unusable in a checked-in fixture: a newline ends the
; one-diagnostic-per-line format the AXDL goldens are read with, a
; carriage return splits a LINE for any reader using universal
; newlines while this compiler counts LF only (so the span gate and
; the compiler would disagree about which line this is on), and a tab
; is refused outright by check-fmt-selfhost's preservation sweep,
; which reads a tab anywhere in formatted output as the indentation
; it bans. One byte with no two-character form anywhere exercises
; every path the three bugs shared.
(macro pick ((pick "ac")
   (:: picked Int)
   (fn (picked) 1)))

(pick 0)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
